  "articleBody": "Deciding whether to tackle garage drywall yourself or call in the experts can be a tough call, but there are definite signs it's time to bring in a professional. If you're dealing with specific fire-rating requirements, especially for walls shared with your home or ceilings beneath habitable rooms, you really want someone who knows the codes and can ensure proper installation with the right materials. Another big one is ceiling height; if you have high ceilings, hanging drywall can be a real challenge and frankly, a bit dangerous without the right equipment and experience. Moisture conditions in your garage also play a huge role. A pro can properly inspect for and address any existing moisture issues before covering them up, which is crucial for the longevity of your drywall. And of course, if permit or code questions pop up – and they often do for new or first-time finished walls – a professional general contractor like Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC can navigate those waters for you. We handle projects big and small throughout the greater Denver area, including Centennial, Littleton, and Castle Rock. Don't hesitate to reach out to us at 303-505-0866 for expert guidance and installation!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
